(178049, 10045, 4055, '<td valign="top">Lovely shot! Perfect in b&amp;w. Perhaps a little too centered for my taste. Overall very well done.</td>', 'Lovely shot! Perfect in b&w. Perhaps a little too centered for my taste. Overall very well done.', '2002-12-25 14:07:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(178080, 9986, 4793, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot, ones of my favorites in this challenge</td>', 'Beautiful shot, ones of my favorites in this challenge', '2002-12-25 16:31:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(178090, 9954, 2158, '<td valign="top">Very clever.</td>', 'Very clever.', '2002-12-25 17:23:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(178094, 10045, 4815, '<td valign="top">Talk about a brilliant B&amp;W study. This is it!. A real first rate classic image. Echos back to those Weston days of the f/64 group. Gorgeous feel of firm softness to those petals. A wee tad hot on some of the highlights ( just my opinion ). Glad you included a couple of token petals. Wish both of those petals were dark ( a minor complaint ). A couple of the waterdrops are lost in the brilliance. But the other 50% of the waterdrops are lovely to behold because of their specular highlights and wee inner droplet shadows that make them feel wet. Personally I would like a little softer lighting arrangement to be a bit kinder and more gradual tones in the shadows. But on the otherhand you may intend for the more harsh graphic look in the first place. And in that case I would be on wrong base. This lighting does illustrate the shape of the individual blossums very well at minor expense of some texture. I feel that this is a distinguished worthy effort that deserves reasonable praise for sincere effort. Continue with your fine work..7</td>', 'Talk about a brilliant B&W study. This is it!. A real first rate classic image. Echos back to those Weston days of the f/64 group. Gorgeous feel of firm softness to those petals. A wee tad hot on some of the highlights ( just my opinion ). Glad you included a couple of token petals. Wish both of those petals were dark ( a minor complaint ). A couple of the waterdrops are lost in the brilliance. But the other 50% of the waterdrops are lovely to behold because of their specular highlights and wee inner droplet shadows that make them feel wet. Personally I would like a little softer lighting arrangement to be a bit kinder and more gradual tones in the shadows. But on the otherhand you may intend for the more harsh graphic look in the first place. And in that case I would be on wrong base. This lighting does illustrate the shape of the individual blossums very well at minor expense of some texture. I feel that this is a distinguished worthy effort that deserves reasonable praise for sincere effort. Continue with your fine work..7', '2002-12-25 19:00:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(178100, 9897, 4815, '<td valign="top">There is a lawsuit against you for hospitalized DPC''ers from intense spasmodic laughing injuries. I am going to significantly upscale your average by insisting you accept a score of 10 for originality.A brilliant humourous concept. Technical performance is basically up to snuff. If a magic wand could be waved I would personally like the following for my 8ftX10ft mural version: The worm emerging a la vertical pose from mother dirt against simulated puffy cloud sky. Handy dandy mirror for that one. The white background is just too clinical for me. ( Nightmares of high school science lab and all that). And perhaps a squirt of water aerosol to freshen up her complexion. I do like the specular highlights on the victim though. Could I have just a hint more texture? Perhaps a slightly lower light angle to bring out those drop dead gorgeous laugh lines (OK wormy wrinkles). This is a premium idea that has delightful hidden charms and many more interesting possibilities worth pursuing. Thank you for such an enjoyable image...6</td>', 'There is a lawsuit against you for hospitalized DPC''ers from intense spasmodic laughing injuries. I am going to significantly upscale your average by insisting you accept a score of 10 for originality.A brilliant humourous concept. Technical performance is basically up to snuff. If a magic wand could be waved I would personally like the following for my 8ftX10ft mural version: The worm emerging a la vertical pose from mother dirt against simulated puffy cloud sky. Handy dandy mirror for that one. The white background is just too clinical for me. ( Nightmares of high school science lab and all that). And perhaps a squirt of water aerosol to freshen up her complexion. I do like the specular highlights on the victim though. Could I have just a hint more texture? Perhaps a slightly lower light angle to bring out those drop dead gorgeous laugh lines (OK wormy wrinkles). This is a premium idea that has delightful hidden charms and many more interesting possibilities worth pursuing. Thank you for such an enjoyable image...6', '2002-12-25 19:19:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(178104, 9926, 4815, '<td valign="top">OK this is not a bad idea. Could I suggest a few things? Just my personal  opinion to be read once before chucking. The number, your photo, the actual shirt and the closet all make sense together. If it was my chioce I would like to zone in on just those four visual items. There seems to be a comflict of colours among the yellowish closet, many hues among the shoeboxes and other clothes. Lots of colors are making my attention wander away from your intent. Could this have been expressed closer to your idea in B&amp;W ? Do you need all of those closet items to express your idea? What do you think of a self portrait wearing the shirt with a big proud smile, for example? Or perhaps a spotlight upon the shirt as you handle it from the closet? This is a good effort. The idea is being communicated. Maybe just a few small changes to have a stronger personal message. I am glad that you entered this image just the same. It talks about a significant experience for you and that is what counts. Good luck and keep shooting!</td>', 'OK this is not a bad idea. Could I suggest a few things? Just my personal  opinion to be read once before chucking. The number, your photo, the actual shirt and the closet all make sense together. If it was my chioce I would like to zone in on just those four visual items. There seems to be a comflict of colours among the yellowish closet, many hues among the shoeboxes and other clothes. Lots of colors are making my attention wander away from your intent. Could this have been expressed closer to your idea in B&W ? Do you need all of those closet items to express your idea? What do you think of a self portrait wearing the shirt with a big proud smile, for example? Or perhaps a spotlight upon the shirt as you handle it from the closet? This is a good effort. The idea is being communicated. Maybe just a few small changes to have a stronger personal message. I am glad that you entered this image just the same. It talks about a significant experience for you and that is what counts. Good luck and keep shooting!', '2002-12-25 19:38:02.000000', NULL, 1),
